                        "glosses": [
                            "In a mimicking or imitative manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07840ff5-4624-43dc-b701-179b408be958",
                                "sense_id": "0f0bfff3-55f8-3b2e-b444-c5f4c271acdc",
                                "text": "mimically represented emotions"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4c08126-8e6c-4965-903a-dfc09ca43a84",
                                "sense_id": "0f0bfff3-55f8-3b2e-b444-c5f4c271acdc",
                                "text": "In the last place, he argues, that if it be lawful to baptize infants without understanding, baptism may be mimically and jocularly administered by boys in play."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7387bbc-0c99-414b-9bb5-fa191ee0be44",
                                "sense_id": "0f0bfff3-55f8-3b2e-b444-c5f4c271acdc",
                                "text": "Be neither mimically in , nor ridiculously out of the fashion ; let your apparel be neat , not chargeable , fitted as well to your estate, years, and profession, as to your person."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aefcfb3b-f352-4957-a2c6-e96338b9165f",
                                "sense_id": "0f0bfff3-55f8-3b2e-b444-c5f4c271acdc",
                                "text": "The script of Stroheim's Greed (1924), despite the encumbrance of inter-titles, demonstrates how much psychology could indeed be portrayed mimically and through a proliferation of perspectival close-ups and reaction shots;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9bb27921-fedb-3994-a70d-3e327f34c5b9",
                        "entry_id": "cf236685-0b5c-31cf-a711-7d66e8c94c7e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a manner that preserves the form and internal structure of an organic substance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ad62747-f669-4492-9113-8ffd55bcbc1f",
                                "sense_id": "9bb27921-fedb-3994-a70d-3e327f34c5b9",
                                "text": "Allochems and preexisting cements may be unreplaced, partially replaced, replaced mimically, or replaced nonmimically."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65ccf679-25f0-41fa-b5be-9dd11aa3e2df",
                                "sense_id": "9bb27921-fedb-3994-a70d-3e327f34c5b9",
                                "text": "The overgrowths have been mimically dolomitized."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25ea5360-417a-45a0-90ab-0cf5a5672b36",
                                "sense_id": "9bb27921-fedb-3994-a70d-3e327f34c5b9",
                                "text": "The echinoid fragments are mimically replaced by silica."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e665c74-d35e-47b4-bb45-cc137ad8f56d",
                                "sense_id": "9bb27921-fedb-3994-a70d-3e327f34c5b9",
                                "text": "If carbonate grains are completely replaced, they may be replaced mimically or nonmimically ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
